Field Type Meaning <code>file</code> string site-absolute path the drawer fetches, e.g. <code>/data/dsge/census/UK_SM11.json</code>. The loader strips the leading <code>/data/</code> and fetches under the app's base path <code>source</code> string repository path the bytes came from — <code>pipeline/census_irfs/&lt;dir&gt;/Taylor.json</code> for a census model, <code>app/public/data/dsge/irfs/&lt;M&gt;/SW.json</code> for an indexed-in-place one <code>title</code> string optional menu display name; only the FRB/US entries carry one. Absent ⇒ show the index key <code>sourceNote</code> string optional provenance label, <code>"MMB rule file"</code> or <code>"MMB census run"</code> (§13.6) <code>sha256</code> string content hash of the shipped file <code>sha256Source</code> string where that hash came from: <code>pipeline/census_irfs/MANIFEST.json</code> for the eight census entries, <code>sha256(app/public/data/dsge/irfs/&lt;M&gt;/SW.json)</code> for the four indexed-in-place ones <code>shocks</code> string[] the usable shocks, in the model's own file order. A shock is usable iff it carries all three common observables and its stacked three-observable, twelve-quarter response path has norm ≥ 1e-9 <code>dropped</code> object[] <code>{shock, reason}</code> for everything excluded. The builder emits two reasons, <code>"zero-response"</code> and <code>"missing-observable"</code>; only the first occurs in the shipped index, on SW07's <code>em</code> and CMR14's <code>e_term</code>. Every other model drops nothing <code>hasOutput</code> bool whether the model exposes an <code>output</code> observable. <code>false</code> disables the menu entry, since <code>output</code> anchors the whole conversion. All twelve shipped entries are <code>true</code> <code>collinearPairs</code> object[] <code>{a, b, cos}</code> for every pair with |cos| &gt; 0.95, <code>cos</code> rounded to six decimals <code>menuHidden</code> bool optional, <code>true</code> on <code>US_FRB22_mcap</code> alone — the entry stays in the index because the licence fixtures reference it, but the drawer menu filters it out (§13.6) <code>classMapKey</code> string optional: the <code>shockClasses.models</code> record to use when it differs from the index key. All three FRB22 entries point at <code>US_FRB22_mcap</code> <code>clusters</code> object[] optional, FRB/US census models only: <code>{id, label, members}</code> (§13.4) <code>defaultNamed</code> string[] optional, clustered models only: the build-time-validated default cluster naming (§13.4) <p>The menu as shipped, with the file facts alongside the index metadata:</p> Index key Usable shocks Dropped Observables in the file Collinear pairs Clusters <code>US_SW07</code> 7 <code>em</code> 71 0 — <code>US_CMR14</code> 9 <code>e_term</code> 395 3 — <code>US_FRB08</code> 2 — 398 0 — <code>US_FRB22</code> 54 — 454 109 23 <code>US_FRB22_var</code> 54 — 449 117 21 <code>US_FRB22_mcap</code> 2 — 454 0 — (menu-hidden) <code>EA_SW03</code> 6 — 86 1 — <code>EA_SWW14</code> 6 — 82 0 — <code>CA_LS07</code> 3 — 38 1 — <code>HK_FP13</code> 5 — 99 2 — <code>BRA_SAMBA08</code> 4 — 71 0 — <code>UK_SM11</code> 3 — 169 0 — <p>The flagged pairs are few enough to list. <code>US_CMR14</code> flags <code>e_sigma</code>–<code>e_gamma</code> (0.997711), <code>e_gamma</code>–<code>e_zetai</code> (0.982712) and <code>e_sigma</code>–<code>e_zetai</code> (0.975082); <code>EA_SW03</code> flags <code>fiscal_</code>–<code>inv_</code> (0.963437); <code>CA_LS07</code> flags <code>markup_</code>–<code>flex_</code> (0.974943); <code>HK_FP13</code> flags <code>interest_</code>–<code>flex_</code> (1.0, an exact duplicate) and <code>markup_</code>–<code>demand_</code> (0.959529). Where a pair is flagged, the split of a contribution within that pair is not identified and the two members should be read jointly; the drawer's one-click "Use all" therefore keeps only one member of each flagged group, and warns if the user names both by hand.</p> <p>Example 1 (<code>index.json</code> — the header, one small entry in full, the rest abridged). We show the shipped file down to the level a consumer needs: the header fields, the class-map block, one complete census entry (<code>UK_SM11</code>, three shocks, no clusters), and the shape of a clustered FRB/US entry. Values are real; the ellipses stand for omitted siblings.</p> <pre><code>{
